.TH YYPARSE 3 "2026-04-02" "IEEE/The Open Group" "POSIX Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
yyparse, yylex, yyerror \- parsing interfaces generated by yacc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "y.tab.h"
.PP
.B int yyparse(void);
.PP
.B int yylex(void);
.PP
.B void yyerror(const char *\fIs\fP);
.PP
.B extern YYSTYPE yylval;
.br
.B extern int yychar;
.br
.B extern int yydebug;
.br
.B extern int yynerrs;
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR yyparse ()
function is generated by the
.BR yacc (1)
parser generator. It serves as the primary entry point to an LALR(1) parser.
When called,
.BR yyparse ()
repeatedly invokes the user-supplied lexical analyzer function
.BR yylex ()
to gather tokens from an input stream and attempts to match them against the structured rules defined in the grammar.
.PP
The user must provide an implementation for
.BR yylex ().
Each call to
.BR yylex ()
must return an integer representing the token type. The lexical analyzer should return
.B 0
or a negative value to signify the end of the input stream. When returning a token,
.BR yylex ()
should assign the semantic value associated with that token to the global variable
.BR yylval .
.PP
If the parser encounters an invalid token sequence that violates the grammar, it invokes the user-supplied
.BR yyerror ()
function, passing a diagnostic string (typically
.BR "syntax error" )
as the parameter
.IR s .
The user's implementation of
.BR yyerror ()
is responsible for reporting the error to standard error, logging mechanisms, or displaying it to the user.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR yyparse ()
function returns
.B 0
if the entire input stream was successfully parsed according to the provided grammar.
It returns
.B 1
if a syntax error occurred that could not be recovered from via error recovery productions, or if a memory exhaustion error occurred internally during parsing.
.SH GLOBAL VARIABLES
.TP
.B YYSTYPE yylval
A union variable used to pass semantic values between the lexical analyzer and the parser.
.TP
.B int yychar
Contains the integer value of the current lookahead token.
.TP
.B int yydebug
If the parser was generated using the
.B \-t
switch, setting this integer variable to a non-zero value enables runtime trace debugging on standard error.
.TP
.B int yynerrs
An integer tracking the cumulative number of syntax errors encountered during the execution of
.BR yyparse ().
.SH ERROR RECOVERY MACROS
Within semantic actions, particularly those associated with the special
.B error
token, the following macros are available:
.TP
.B yyerrok
Resets the parser's internal error state, indicating that error recovery is complete and standard parsing should resume.
.TP
.B yyclearin
Discards the current lookahead token. This is often used during error recovery when the lookahead token caused the error and must be bypassed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yacc (1),
.BR yacc_grammar (5),
.BR lex (1)
